1
00:00:01,368 --> 00:00:04,337
Welcome! It's been a while.

2
00:00:05,071 --> 00:00:06,639
What can I get for you today?

3
00:00:09,376 --> 00:00:10,777
Okay. Thank you very much.

4
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:17,150
Oh no...

5
00:00:54,587 --> 00:00:56,389
Michiko! Sorry to keep you waiting.

6
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,126
They're fresh out of the oven.
Come over here!

7
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:01,027
Okay.

8
00:01:10,336 --> 00:01:13,273
What's up with you?
You're strangely generous today.

9
00:01:13,339 --> 00:01:15,909
What do you mean "strangely"?
Eat up everyone!

10
00:01:15,975 --> 00:01:17,343
I think it's going to snow.

11
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,445
Reach!

12
00:01:18,511 --> 00:01:19,712
LOOK!

13
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:21,981
I WIN!

14
00:01:22,048 --> 00:01:22,882
LOOK AT THIS!

15
00:01:25,819 --> 00:01:27,153
- Goodness.
- What is it?

16
00:01:27,854 --> 00:01:30,723
- Did you really?
- Gosh!

17
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,829
What is it?

18
00:01:36,796 --> 00:01:39,833
- Man, what should I do.
- Why is that?

19
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:41,201
What is going on?

20
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,303
- Can you believe it?
- Gosh!

21
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:49,209
I operated on this girl the other day,

22
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:52,679
and I found this online. Saying,
"This is Dr. Kaji, who operated on me."

23
00:01:52,745 --> 00:01:55,381
She's 23! 23!

24
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:57,617
You are...

25
00:01:59,252 --> 00:02:00,386
too naive.

26
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,256
Sorry?

27
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:09,762
Doctors shouldn't get involved
personally with patients so easily.

28
00:02:09,829 --> 00:02:11,264
No, but this...

29
00:02:11,331 --> 00:02:14,968
That type of women can
turn out to be a stalker.

30
00:02:15,034 --> 00:02:16,169
Stalker?

31
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,370
Oh, hey it's updated.

32
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:21,474
She said that you are the coolest doctor
at Teito Medical University Hospital!

33
00:02:21,541 --> 00:02:24,511
Retweet it right now! Spread the
information to the whole world!

34
00:02:24,577 --> 00:02:26,112
Are you really sure?

35
00:02:27,113 --> 00:02:28,882
THE COOLEST DOCTOR AT HOSPITAL

36
00:02:29,916 --> 00:02:30,950
I decline.

37
00:02:37,957 --> 00:02:40,927
If you are sincerely thinking
about your future as a doctor,

38
00:02:42,362 --> 00:02:46,166
I suggest you act carefully.

39
00:02:52,205 --> 00:02:55,275
You look beautiful today, as always.

40
00:02:56,809 --> 00:02:58,645
- Thank you.
- What?

41
00:02:58,711 --> 00:03:01,681
Dr. Daimon. You have a visitor.

42
00:03:02,148 --> 00:03:03,183
Who is it?

43
00:03:03,616 --> 00:03:04,617
Dr. Daimon,

44
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:08,154
last night…did you pick up a wallet?

45
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:14,494
Hey, Demon, did you steal it?

46
00:03:24,904 --> 00:03:26,906
Are you the one who found my wallet?

47
00:03:27,473 --> 00:03:28,374
Yes.

48
00:03:28,441 --> 00:03:30,310
I got a call from the police.

49
00:03:30,843 --> 00:03:31,778
Thank you very much.

50
00:03:32,278 --> 00:03:33,446
It was very helpful.

51
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:34,514
No problem.

52
00:03:35,915 --> 00:03:38,251
You can leave it here.

53
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:42,121
You can…leave it here.

54
00:03:43,122 --> 00:03:44,591
Let go.

55
00:03:44,657 --> 00:03:45,925
Let go!

56
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:47,860
I said let go!

57
00:03:52,532 --> 00:03:54,767
Michiko! Do you want to
take home these leftovers?

58
00:03:56,302 --> 00:03:57,804
Free for you, take them.

59
00:03:58,338 --> 00:04:00,106
Come on!

60
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,876
This isn't much,
but it's a token of my gratitude.

61
00:04:07,146 --> 00:04:09,382
I love the taiyaki from that store too.

62
00:04:10,049 --> 00:04:11,184
Well, then.

63
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,352
Thank you.

64
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:13,820
- Thank you.
- The doctors...

65
00:04:13,886 --> 00:04:17,490
Hospital Chief Hiruma,
will now commence his rounds.

66
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:43,016
Hey, now that I'm at a hospital,

67
00:04:43,082 --> 00:04:46,552
maybe I will make an appointment
for a health checkup here.

68
00:04:46,986 --> 00:04:47,954
Really?

69
00:04:48,021 --> 00:04:51,591
Hey, she wants to make
an appointment for a health checkup.

70
00:04:51,658 --> 00:04:54,994
<i>This is the story of a lone wolf</i>
<i>woman doctor.</i>

71
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:59,499
You have that luxurious course
which takes several days, correct?

72
00:04:59,565 --> 00:05:00,700
The best one.

73
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:03,002
Yes. Please come this way.

74
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:07,774
<i>In 2016, the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

75
00:05:08,241 --> 00:05:10,443
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

76
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:12,345
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

77
00:05:13,446 --> 00:05:17,617
<i>Famous hospitals use their brand power</i>
<i>to push into the world.</i>

78
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,820
<i>On the other hand, highly skilled surgeons</i>

79
00:05:20,887 --> 00:05:24,123
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary</i>
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

80
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:27,527
<i>The world of medicine has entered</i>

81
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:31,964
<i>into the global world</i>
<i>of survival of the fittest.</i>

82
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:39,072
<i>In the midst of it,</i>
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>

83
00:05:39,138 --> 00:05:42,608
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>
<i>in other words, lone doctors.</i>

84
00:05:46,212 --> 00:05:48,147
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

85
00:05:48,715 --> 00:05:52,785
<i>Despising the herd mentality,</i>
<i>authority and institutional restraints...</i>

86
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:56,723
<i>Her solo weapons are her license and</i>

87
00:05:56,789 --> 00:05:58,057
<i>the skills she has earned.</i>

88
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:01,561
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

89
00:06:01,627 --> 00:06:04,831
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

90
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:36,696
I'm in charge of all schedules

91
00:06:36,763 --> 00:06:38,431
for the special checkup course.

92
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:39,766
You know that, right?

93
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,501
No.

94
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,704
Let me see that, Minami.

95
00:06:45,538 --> 00:06:50,076
From the 22nd to the 24th,
Mr. Kuga, the councilor,

96
00:06:50,143 --> 00:06:52,779
has his special checkup
appointment already.

97
00:06:52,845 --> 00:06:54,480
It's definitely double booking.

98
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:56,549
- Oh really.
- What do you mean by that?

99
00:06:56,983 --> 00:07:00,486
To take full care for the councilor,
the internal medicine team

100
00:07:00,953 --> 00:07:02,555
is out of hands at the moment.

101
00:07:02,622 --> 00:07:05,558
This special checkup
is not for any regular patients.

102
00:07:05,625 --> 00:07:08,194
I should have dealt with this.
I apologise.

103
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,629
Pull yourself together.

104
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:14,167
Weren't you the one who said
it'd help improve the value...

105
00:07:14,233 --> 00:07:16,102
of our hospital if Mr. Kuga's

106
00:07:16,169 --> 00:07:17,370
checkup goes well?

107
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,238
- I apologise.
- Can I go now?

108
00:07:19,305 --> 00:07:20,973
Seriously.

109
00:07:21,307 --> 00:07:24,177
Having our schedule
thrown off by some surgeon

110
00:07:24,243 --> 00:07:26,012
is a real inconvenience.

111
00:07:26,345 --> 00:07:28,714
To begin with, this hospital
would not accept

112
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,316
a patient for health check

113
00:07:30,383 --> 00:07:33,719
without a recommendation letter
or clear background.

114
00:07:33,786 --> 00:07:35,455
What was I supposed to...

115
00:07:35,521 --> 00:07:37,924
- What if something happens?
- What do you mean?

116
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:40,126
Medical exam cannot be
covered by insurance.

117
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:43,830
Furthermore, our special course
is very expensive.

118
00:07:44,664 --> 00:07:46,466
We don't know if she can afford it.

119
00:07:46,532 --> 00:07:48,668
So that's what you meant.

120
00:07:49,202 --> 00:07:50,336
Just don't accept her.

121
00:07:50,403 --> 00:07:51,838
That won't do.

122
00:07:51,904 --> 00:07:54,240
If word gets out that
we turned down a patient

123
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:56,843
after accepting once,
rumors will start flying.

124
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:58,244
It will impact
the reputation of this hospital.

125
00:07:58,311 --> 00:07:59,846
Can I leave now?

126
00:08:00,379 --> 00:08:01,481
Michiko Daimon!

127
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:06,419
You take responsibility as her guardian!

128
00:08:09,055 --> 00:08:09,922
I decline.

129
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:15,027
You won't get away
with it this time, you know.

130
00:08:16,095 --> 00:08:17,230
Why not?

131
00:08:17,296 --> 00:08:21,701
What if that woman you don't even know,

132
00:08:21,767 --> 00:08:26,038
doesn't pay the checkup fee? What happens?

133
00:08:26,105 --> 00:08:27,306
I don't know.

134
00:08:27,373 --> 00:08:30,176
As her guardian, you are going to
have to pay for her.

135
00:08:30,243 --> 00:08:32,245
That is what may happen.

136
00:08:32,311 --> 00:08:33,312
What?

137
00:08:33,379 --> 00:08:38,484
In short, our office will
have to pay all of the fees.

138
00:08:38,551 --> 00:08:41,554
The entire fees for the special
medical checkup.

139
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:44,423
The special course
is really something else.

140
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:47,460
Everyone keeps talking
about this special course...

141
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,928
What is so great about it?

142
00:08:48,995 --> 00:08:54,100
If it were a meat, it would be
a full course of A5 Kobe beef.

143
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:55,001
What?

144
00:08:55,067 --> 00:08:56,402
A full-time concierge

145
00:08:56,469 --> 00:08:59,171
takes care of everything like a hotel.

146
00:08:59,238 --> 00:09:03,476
The room is a special private room.
Food is catered by a fancy restaurant.

147
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:07,280
There is no waiting time, and you
won't ever run into other patients.

148
00:09:07,346 --> 00:09:10,082
Three whole days

149
00:09:10,149 --> 00:09:11,350
for total luxury.

150
00:09:12,418 --> 00:09:14,554
That's truly amazing.

151
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:19,792
What? I'm sorry I didn't know!

152
00:09:19,859 --> 00:09:24,964
This is a result of your reckless actions.
Resign yourself to it.

153
00:09:26,699 --> 00:09:28,501
What are you doing here anyway?

154
00:09:29,001 --> 00:09:31,370
Well she is a special customer after all,

155
00:09:31,437 --> 00:09:34,407
so I should introduce myself
as the Surgery Department Chief.

156
00:09:34,774 --> 00:09:37,376
I heard she is quite a beauty.

157
00:09:39,779 --> 00:09:41,714
This service is
for a special course guest.

158
00:09:41,781 --> 00:09:45,017
Meals are catered by
Joubert Robuchon Hotel.

159
00:09:48,721 --> 00:09:50,523
Misae is her name, huh?

160
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:55,127
Come to think of it, this woman
was staring at you the other day.

161
00:09:57,863 --> 00:10:01,300
- Goodness. Gosh, what do I do.
- Stop it.

162
00:10:01,367 --> 00:10:06,906
Decades ago…when I was
working at Onarimon hospital,

163
00:10:07,406 --> 00:10:10,843
there was a woman named Misae...

164
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:14,580
who I saved during an ulcer operation.

165
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:20,519
Well, it's an old story. And that Misae...

166
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,288
Coming in.

167
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:26,759
- Huh?
- Oh my goodness,

168
00:10:26,826 --> 00:10:29,362
Dr. Saionji!

169
00:10:29,428 --> 00:10:32,064
What a coincidence!

170
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,901
It's been a long time.

171
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,937
Hello.

172
00:10:38,004 --> 00:10:41,841
Who would've thought
we'd see each other again like this!

173
00:10:42,441 --> 00:10:45,277
You look…as beautiful as ever.

174
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:48,848
- Do you know her?
- Yes, we...

175
00:10:51,017 --> 00:10:53,386
- dated a long time ago.
- No, well...

176
00:10:56,122 --> 00:10:59,125
I had no idea you were married.

177
00:11:00,526 --> 00:11:01,927
Well, that is...

178
00:11:04,363 --> 00:11:08,267
It's time for a conference.
I'll leave the rest to you.

179
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,435
An affair?

180
00:11:10,436 --> 00:11:11,303
Be quiet.

181
00:11:13,472 --> 00:11:14,674
He had an affair.

182
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:18,010
Can't wait for dessert.

183
00:11:30,956 --> 00:11:32,158
What is she up to?

184
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:44,904
I can't do this anymore!
It's so boring! I hate this!

185
00:11:46,138 --> 00:11:50,743
I hate this! All these back-to-back
surgeries are killing me.

186
00:11:51,777 --> 00:11:57,516
Miss Demon looks tired from
taking care of the VIP patient.

187
00:11:58,918 --> 00:12:00,086
- I need to cut.
- What?

188
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:05,324
Stop it! No! Hey! Stop her!

189
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,026
- Stop, I...
- Excuse me.

190
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:09,795
Dr. Daimon! The test results for

191
00:12:09,862 --> 00:12:11,831
Miss Misae Suyama are ready.

192
00:12:12,832 --> 00:12:14,066
All right.

193
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:26,746
WHITE BLOOD: 19000 RED BLOOD: 388

194
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:39,692
Is this...?

195
00:12:44,063 --> 00:12:45,865
WARNING: RADIOACTIVE AREA

196
00:12:49,802 --> 00:12:52,505
What do you suppose this is?

197
00:12:53,005 --> 00:12:54,740
Run an MRI, too.

198
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:57,076
Huh? But...

199
00:12:59,645 --> 00:13:02,515
Hey, hey, hey...
Dr. Daimon what are you doing?

200
00:13:02,581 --> 00:13:03,549
CT.

201
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:08,187
Council Mr. Kuga has an
appointment scheduled for this time.

202
00:13:08,254 --> 00:13:10,489
- Right?
- Yes sir, but she forced me to...

203
00:13:10,556 --> 00:13:11,724
This is an emergency.

204
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:14,026
She is not an emergency
case nor a special patient!

205
00:13:14,093 --> 00:13:15,394
She's here for a health check!

206
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:17,630
There is a chance she can
turn into an emergency case.

207
00:13:17,696 --> 00:13:19,131
I'd still like to see the MRI.

208
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:21,834
Like I said, Kuga has an MRI after this...

209
00:13:21,901 --> 00:13:23,536
- Hurry up and get the MRI!
- Got it!

210
00:13:23,602 --> 00:13:24,470
Hey.

211
00:13:24,537 --> 00:13:26,939
EMERGENCY CONFERENCE

212
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:33,245
I heard she's Dr. Saionji's lover.

213
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,848
You mean his ex-girlfriend?

214
00:13:39,852 --> 00:13:41,387
It was an affair.

215
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,165
- What is that?
- It's huge.

216
00:13:53,632 --> 00:13:55,134
I've never seen a tumor that big.

217
00:13:55,201 --> 00:13:56,302
Could it be pancreatic cancer?

218
00:13:57,436 --> 00:13:59,572
That might be possible, but...

219
00:13:59,638 --> 00:14:02,074
It's too large.

220
00:14:02,474 --> 00:14:05,177
When pancreatic cancer gets this large,

221
00:14:05,878 --> 00:14:07,379
it's usually accompanied with pain

222
00:14:07,713 --> 00:14:09,348
and would also interfere
with the patient's daily life.

223
00:14:09,415 --> 00:14:10,816
She needs to be hospitalised.

224
00:14:11,283 --> 00:14:14,620
Daimon, what is your opinion?

225
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:23,529
Daimon?

226
00:14:34,573 --> 00:14:35,608
I have no idea.

227
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:40,179
No idea is not an answer.

228
00:14:40,246 --> 00:14:42,481
I won't know unless I cut her open.

229
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:45,084
Here we go. You trying to
get me to let you do surgery.

230
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,619
- Let me do the operation.
- Excuse me?

231
00:14:47,253 --> 00:14:49,822
It could be a soft tissue tumor that grew.

232
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:53,192
If that is so, Dr. Kitano,
you be in charge.

233
00:14:53,259 --> 00:14:54,126
I am in charge of...

234
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:56,562
I have operated on
soft tissue tumours 35 times.

235
00:14:56,629 --> 00:14:58,597
I should be the one to cut it.

236
00:14:58,664 --> 00:15:03,502
Okay, I got it.
Dr. Kitano will do the operation.

237
00:15:05,337 --> 00:15:08,574
But if this tumor

238
00:15:08,974 --> 00:15:12,344
grows even bigger...

239
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:15,481
this clinical case would be unprecedented.

240
00:15:15,547 --> 00:15:19,018
It may be the first case
of its kind in the world.

241
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:22,655
It will be a great appealing point...
for Toutei University hospital.

242
00:15:23,689 --> 00:15:26,992
So a surgery that would possibly
gain attention of the world,

243
00:15:27,059 --> 00:15:30,462
has to be done by a
doctor who's officially

244
00:15:30,529 --> 00:15:32,865
affiliated with this hospital,
don't you think?

245
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,333
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

246
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,368
No, I want to do it. I will cut it.

247
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:37,803
Come on.

248
00:15:41,907 --> 00:15:43,709
- Dr. Saionji.
- Yes?

249
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,744
So what's going on with
your relationship with that mistress?

250
00:15:45,811 --> 00:15:46,845
Oh...huh?

251
00:15:46,912 --> 00:15:48,981
I mean, well that is...

252
00:15:49,048 --> 00:15:50,816
Your affair with the patient.

253
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,852
Now is not a good time for us to discuss.

254
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,656
Reckless behavior can prove fatal,
you know?

255
00:15:58,023 --> 00:15:59,558
Did you get it resolved?

256
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,194
Of course.

257
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:03,896
Things with that woman,

258
00:16:04,563 --> 00:16:08,634
I mean, the patient.

259
00:16:09,401 --> 00:16:14,473
I have nothing to do with her.
Now then. If you'll excuse me now.

260
00:16:14,907 --> 00:16:17,042
How about her feelings?

261
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:18,644
What?

262
00:16:19,078 --> 00:16:23,148
There is something about
her wanting to receive...

263
00:16:23,582 --> 00:16:24,883
her health check here.

264
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:31,790
What? I just happened to find her wallet.

265
00:16:31,857 --> 00:16:35,728
Including that, it is possible that
everything was a set up?

266
00:16:35,794 --> 00:16:37,396
Huh, what? Which means what?

267
00:16:37,463 --> 00:16:39,331
You are saying this patient

268
00:16:39,398 --> 00:16:43,569
got came to this particular hospital
with the intention of...

269
00:16:43,635 --> 00:16:44,903
doing what?

270
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:47,873
Uh, I…have no idea.

271
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,775
- I have a question.
- Yes.

272
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,411
Was it before…or after...

273
00:16:52,478 --> 00:16:59,251
the operation that you…uh dated her?

274
00:17:00,319 --> 00:17:03,789
Well, that was…the latter, of course.

275
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:05,257
I see.

276
00:17:05,324 --> 00:17:06,425
Is that an issue?

277
00:17:06,492 --> 00:17:09,862
Well, I was just curious.

278
00:17:13,465 --> 00:17:15,934
Remember, I'm the one
performing the surgery.

279
00:17:18,971 --> 00:17:21,240
Abandoned women

280
00:17:21,306 --> 00:17:22,975
are so scary.

281
00:17:23,041 --> 00:17:24,043
Oh really.

282
00:17:24,109 --> 00:17:26,745
Well I think it's just a coincidence.

283
00:17:26,812 --> 00:17:28,313
I hope so.

284
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:35,320
But Michiko, you felt uneasy like she
had something else in mind, right?

285
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:36,655
Kind of.

286
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:39,691
But it doesn't matter anymore.
No use thinking about it.

287
00:17:39,758 --> 00:17:41,693
I have no idea!

288
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:47,633
By the way, what bothers me…is the
size of the tumour shown in the MRI.

289
00:17:47,699 --> 00:17:49,068
Right.

290
00:17:49,134 --> 00:17:50,102
Pancreatic cancer,

291
00:17:50,169 --> 00:17:51,603
soft tissue tumour,

292
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:53,839
intraperitoneal abscess,

293
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:56,275
- none of them fits at all.
- Exactly.

294
00:17:56,842 --> 00:18:00,446
What about leiomyosarcoma? A large one.

295
00:18:00,512 --> 00:18:03,615
I thought about that, but
no evidence of ulcer or necrosis.

296
00:18:03,682 --> 00:18:04,817
That's impossible.

297
00:18:04,883 --> 00:18:06,785
Then what is it?

298
00:18:06,852 --> 00:18:10,722
It means you will have to wait
until she is cut opened.

299
00:18:12,658 --> 00:18:15,060
I really wanted to do the surgery.

300
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:17,563
Then why don't you be his assistant?

301
00:18:17,629 --> 00:18:21,733
No way! Who would want to assist a weird
guy that speaks weird English.

302
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:24,436
Oh my god! Amazing.

303
00:18:24,503 --> 00:18:26,271
Hello, everybody.

304
00:18:26,738 --> 00:18:27,940
How are you doing?

305
00:18:30,409 --> 00:18:32,945
Let's begin the distal pancreatectomy.

306
00:18:33,011 --> 00:18:33,979
Let's do our best.

307
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:35,581
Let's do our best.

308
00:18:35,981 --> 00:18:39,818
I'm really glad that you're assisting me.

309
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:41,120
Thanks.

310
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:44,156
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

311
00:18:46,258 --> 00:18:47,292
Incision.

312
00:18:55,067 --> 00:18:56,735
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

313
00:19:15,787 --> 00:19:17,556
How long since you broke up with her?

314
00:19:20,325 --> 00:19:23,862
Probably around…20 years.

315
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:26,698
20 years?

316
00:19:27,399 --> 00:19:30,102
A woman who you left 20 years ago...
comes to see you,

317
00:19:30,169 --> 00:19:33,872
after waiting so long for a man
she knew would never come at a bar alone.

318
00:19:33,939 --> 00:19:37,276
- How melodramatic. It's like a soap opera!
- Stop it.

319
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:42,748
- I am still alone. So lonely...
- Stop it!

320
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,221
What's this?

321
00:19:54,092 --> 00:19:55,194
No way.

322
00:19:56,161 --> 00:19:56,995
This is...

323
00:19:59,565 --> 00:20:00,599
a gauzeoma.

324
00:20:02,935 --> 00:20:04,670
Gauzeoma?

325
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:06,171
What?

326
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:10,676
Gauzeoma.

327
00:20:11,977 --> 00:20:13,745
Gauzeoma?

328
00:20:13,812 --> 00:20:14,980
Gauzeoma?

329
00:20:16,949 --> 00:20:18,483
What's gauzeoma?

330
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,054
A tumour produced
by gauze left in the body.

331
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:25,691
In other words,
during the previous surgery,

332
00:20:26,792 --> 00:20:29,328
a piece of gauze was left in the stomach.

333
00:20:40,105 --> 00:20:41,173
So that means,

334
00:20:43,008 --> 00:20:44,543
it's a medical malpractice.

335
00:20:51,950 --> 00:20:52,884
Close up!

336
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,854
You need to close!

337
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,456
Right away!

338
00:20:57,522 --> 00:20:58,790
Stop the operation!

339
00:21:02,194 --> 00:21:04,763
I will now detach the tumour.

340
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:05,664
Okay.

341
00:21:05,731 --> 00:21:07,332
I told you to stop now!

342
00:21:07,733 --> 00:21:08,967
It is inoperable!

343
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:12,938
Inoperable? Why? This is an easy surgery.

344
00:21:13,005 --> 00:21:14,906
Stop complaining, Daimon!

345
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:16,842
Close up, right now!

346
00:21:18,143 --> 00:21:19,211
I don't get it.

347
00:21:20,145 --> 00:21:21,880
Hey, move.

348
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:22,981
Take her.

349
00:21:23,415 --> 00:21:24,549
Get her out!

350
00:21:24,883 --> 00:21:28,086
Get off from me! Stop it!

351
00:21:28,153 --> 00:21:32,357
Let go of me!

352
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:39,865
Hey,

353
00:21:40,866 --> 00:21:42,334
why is it inoperable?

354
00:21:43,001 --> 00:21:46,505
Taking out the gauze
is something anyone can do.

355
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:49,908
What?

356
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:54,212
Well, this is a university hospital
with authority, you know.

357
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:55,380
So what?

358
00:21:56,281 --> 00:22:00,285
It may not mean anything
to a freelancer like you,

359
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:02,754
but it's a very delicate situation.

360
00:22:04,523 --> 00:22:06,725
The surgery chief of
Toutei University Hospital...

361
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:10,062
left gauze in a patient's stomach.

362
00:22:10,128 --> 00:22:11,430
It can never be made public.

363
00:22:18,203 --> 00:22:22,174
There's an urgent meeting
for the surgery team.

364
00:22:27,913 --> 00:22:31,717
You really did something terrible
this time, didn't you, Chief Saionji?

365
00:22:31,783 --> 00:22:32,951
Yes.

366
00:22:33,418 --> 00:22:35,220
It was 20 years ago.

367
00:22:35,954 --> 00:22:38,824
How could she have been okay so far?

368
00:22:38,890 --> 00:22:40,425
That's unpardonable mistake.

369
00:22:41,993 --> 00:22:44,129
Where is Dr. Daimon?

370
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:51,536
He left a piece of gauze in my stomach?

371
00:22:52,304 --> 00:22:53,138
Yes.

372
00:23:12,157 --> 00:23:13,158
In here?

373
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:17,095
- Right.
- I got it during my surgery 20 years ago?

374
00:23:20,599 --> 00:23:21,800
It was you.

375
00:23:24,669 --> 00:23:25,604
That's...

376
00:23:28,106 --> 00:23:29,040
correct.

377
00:23:35,046 --> 00:23:36,148
What should I do, then?

378
00:23:37,315 --> 00:23:39,618
I will take it out during the surgery.

379
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:52,197
I thought we were over long ago,

380
00:23:53,732 --> 00:23:56,334
but we are somehow weirdly entangled.

381
00:24:01,006 --> 00:24:02,774
You told her?

382
00:24:02,841 --> 00:24:04,576
- To the patient?
- Yes.

383
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:08,713
Come here, to the front.

384
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:11,383
Come to the front.
What is your name again?

385
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,417
Saionji.

386
00:24:12,484 --> 00:24:16,655
Saionji, come here. You told her that...

387
00:24:16,721 --> 00:24:20,125
Dr. Saionji…left gauze in her stomach?

388
00:24:20,192 --> 00:24:21,259
What's the matter?

389
00:24:21,326 --> 00:24:22,627
Demon!

390
00:24:22,694 --> 00:24:24,129
You're a part-timer, right?

391
00:24:24,196 --> 00:24:25,263
Freelancer.

392
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:28,300
Stop causing trouble.

393
00:24:28,366 --> 00:24:29,334
Perhaps, this is...

394
00:24:29,401 --> 00:24:30,435
What?

395
00:24:30,502 --> 00:24:32,370
- a revenge.
- A revenge?

396
00:24:34,706 --> 00:24:37,209
She might've found out
about the gauze in her body...

397
00:24:37,876 --> 00:24:40,946
through a medical checkup
in other hospital.

398
00:24:41,546 --> 00:24:43,014
And she took advantage of it.

399
00:24:43,081 --> 00:24:45,417
Hey, that's too absurd...

400
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:49,721
At the time, Misae was an hostess...

401
00:24:49,788 --> 00:24:52,491
She was? Which club did she work at?

402
00:24:52,557 --> 00:24:54,426
- Ginza.
- I see.

403
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:56,528
- Why?
- Just out of curiosity.

404
00:24:56,595 --> 00:24:57,829
Sorry, go ahead.

405
00:24:58,697 --> 00:24:59,865
Due to her mismanagement,

406
00:24:59,931 --> 00:25:05,003
her cosmetics company went bust...

407
00:25:05,070 --> 00:25:07,038
leaving her a large debt.

408
00:25:07,739 --> 00:25:10,642
She might be still suffering
from the debt.

409
00:25:11,276 --> 00:25:13,044
So she's trying to use me...

410
00:25:13,111 --> 00:25:15,680
No, she's trying to use Toutei hospital...

411
00:25:15,747 --> 00:25:17,949
to rip off nicely.

412
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:19,985
That would be terrible!

413
00:25:20,051 --> 00:25:21,853
Listen.

414
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,655
I'm trying to get a solution.

415
00:25:24,155 --> 00:25:26,091
- Just be quiet.
- Yes sir.

416
00:25:26,157 --> 00:25:27,526
We need to operate right away!

417
00:25:27,592 --> 00:25:30,428
Like I said,
we need to do what's best for...

418
00:25:30,495 --> 00:25:32,697
What's best is the patient!

419
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:36,468
I will do it.

420
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:37,469
Wait.

421
00:25:37,936 --> 00:25:38,937
Wait.

422
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:43,975
- Dr. Saionji!
- Yes?

423
00:25:44,042 --> 00:25:47,479
Your disrespect for women caused this.

424
00:25:48,179 --> 00:25:49,014
That's not...

425
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,215
For now,

426
00:25:51,917 --> 00:25:54,452
we will try to keep this quiet.

427
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:59,024
There's only a limited number
of people who are aware of this.

428
00:26:01,660 --> 00:26:04,329
I am very grateful.
I knew you could handle it,

429
00:26:04,963 --> 00:26:09,968
Deputy Director Kubo.

430
00:26:10,035 --> 00:26:12,470
If you have time to do this,

431
00:26:13,305 --> 00:26:16,775
you should come up with countermeasures.

432
00:26:16,841 --> 00:26:18,543
Isn't that your job?

433
00:26:25,850 --> 00:26:27,485
What a creepy woman she is.

434
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:31,623
This is horrible.

435
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:34,125
So that is...

436
00:26:35,226 --> 00:26:37,095
a gauzeoma, right?

437
00:26:39,397 --> 00:26:43,368
You forgot something
that you should never forget.

438
00:26:44,135 --> 00:26:45,804
Moreover, you are outnumbered.

439
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:47,572
You must feel terrible.

440
00:26:50,241 --> 00:26:53,111
It is only time before you are abandoned.

441
00:27:03,021 --> 00:27:05,156
I heard Dr. Saionji had an affair!

442
00:27:05,690 --> 00:27:08,193
- Can you believe it?
- He's horrible!

443
00:27:20,205 --> 00:27:23,408
Well, Dr. Saionji asked for it.

444
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:27,946
But who would have thought something this
long ago would catch up with him now.

445
00:27:30,115 --> 00:27:33,485
This does look like cancer
just from the image.

446
00:27:33,551 --> 00:27:37,088
They still used X-seamed gauze
at that time.

447
00:27:37,155 --> 00:27:40,759
As it's been 20 years,
it must've stuck to the organ.

448
00:27:41,192 --> 00:27:42,560
How are you going to remove it?

449
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:45,096
This is...

450
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:48,667
What?

451
00:27:52,604 --> 00:27:53,471
What's wrong?

452
00:27:55,940 --> 00:27:56,808
Hey!

453
00:27:58,076 --> 00:27:59,044
What is going on?

454
00:28:03,214 --> 00:28:05,116
It is inoperable after all.

455
00:28:07,819 --> 00:28:08,720
Hey!

456
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:11,423
- Inject the dye.
- Okay.

457
00:28:14,159 --> 00:28:16,695
What's happening? Is it bad?

458
00:28:16,761 --> 00:28:17,829
<i>Don't talk.</i>

459
00:28:21,299 --> 00:28:22,434
- From another angle.
- Okay.

460
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:30,542
The countermeasure we'll take...

461
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:35,146
is to prevent the information
from leaking out of the hospital,

462
00:28:35,647 --> 00:28:37,148
especially to the media.

463
00:28:37,649 --> 00:28:41,753
Minami, do you have a plan for that?

464
00:28:43,888 --> 00:28:46,524
In regards to the operation 20 years ago,

465
00:28:46,591 --> 00:28:50,328
we'll change the records
by removing Dr. Saionji's name...

466
00:28:50,395 --> 00:28:53,031
and adding the name of another doctor.

467
00:28:53,098 --> 00:28:54,466
Isn't it...

468
00:28:55,934 --> 00:28:57,635
a fabrication?

469
00:28:59,037 --> 00:29:00,371
That's illegal.

470
00:29:00,705 --> 00:29:02,407
There is a large risk,

471
00:29:03,007 --> 00:29:05,410
but it is unavoidable in order to

472
00:29:05,477 --> 00:29:07,345
- protect the hospital's reputation.
- Yes, it's unavoidable.

473
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,613
That is true.

474
00:29:10,081 --> 00:29:12,751
I didn't hear any of this.

475
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:15,820
Please continue after I leave the room.

476
00:29:18,556 --> 00:29:20,425
- Hey!
- I didn't call for you.

477
00:29:20,492 --> 00:29:22,761
And I will not ask for you.

478
00:29:22,827 --> 00:29:25,063
I would like to perform
an emergency operation.

479
00:29:25,130 --> 00:29:27,232
She will die if we don't.

480
00:29:31,569 --> 00:29:33,938
EMERGENCY CONFERENCE

481
00:29:34,005 --> 00:29:35,039
Look at this.

482
00:29:36,975 --> 00:29:39,544
20 years ago at Onarimon hospital,

483
00:29:40,044 --> 00:29:43,948
a doctor left a piece of gauze in the body
of the patient during surgery.

484
00:29:44,949 --> 00:29:47,852
You really made a mess.

485
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:51,656
Now, 20 years later,
a gauzeoma has been formed...

486
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:54,125
and is acting as a foreign object,

487
00:29:54,192 --> 00:29:56,060
being stuck to the organs and tissues.

488
00:29:56,127 --> 00:29:57,262
We know that.

489
00:29:57,328 --> 00:29:58,396
It's really bad.

490
00:29:58,463 --> 00:29:59,497
What are you talking about?

491
00:29:59,998 --> 00:30:03,401
It's not that difficult
to remove a gauzeoma.

492
00:30:04,002 --> 00:30:06,104
Didn't you try to continue on?

493
00:30:07,572 --> 00:30:09,908
The inoperable announcement was correct.

494
00:30:09,974 --> 00:30:11,342
What?

495
00:30:11,943 --> 00:30:14,779
You finally began to understand
how organisations run.

496
00:30:14,846 --> 00:30:17,182
So you have learning ability at least.

497
00:30:17,248 --> 00:30:18,783
Shut it and listen.

498
00:30:19,617 --> 00:30:21,753
If I had continued,

499
00:30:23,221 --> 00:30:24,222
she might have died.

500
00:30:24,289 --> 00:30:25,490
What do you mean?

501
00:30:25,557 --> 00:30:27,158
Look at this image.

502
00:30:29,027 --> 00:30:31,162
In actuality, there is a false aneurysm...

503
00:30:31,563 --> 00:30:34,899
which is about to rupture
right behind the gauzeoma

504
00:30:36,134 --> 00:30:37,068
Here.

505
00:30:37,602 --> 00:30:41,339
It is a hematoma attached to
a blood vessel and the gauzeoma.

506
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:43,441
In other words,

507
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:47,612
if I had forcefully taken the
gauzeoma out during surgery,

508
00:30:47,979 --> 00:30:49,514
the artery would have ruptured...

509
00:30:50,315 --> 00:30:52,650
and the patient would have
died from bleeding.

510
00:30:55,053 --> 00:30:58,189
This false aneurysm has probably
been there for a long time.

511
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:01,593
The reason for it not rupturing until now,

512
00:31:02,961 --> 00:31:05,697
is because it is intertwined
with the gauze.

513
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:10,802
In other words, the gauzeoma
saved the patient's life.

514
00:31:11,636 --> 00:31:12,704
Goodness.

515
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:14,706
That is so unbelievable.

516
00:31:23,514 --> 00:31:24,716
I see.

517
00:31:27,352 --> 00:31:32,023
The gauze...
that Dr. Saionji forgot to remove,

518
00:31:33,491 --> 00:31:36,861
kept me alive so far, right?

519
00:31:40,098 --> 00:31:42,333
Well, that could be one way to put it.

520
00:31:49,574 --> 00:31:53,177
If you leave it as it is, I can
continue living like before, right?

521
00:31:57,382 --> 00:31:59,918
I will continue to live
with the gauze in my body.

522
00:32:00,952 --> 00:32:01,819
Can I?

523
00:32:02,353 --> 00:32:03,488
No.

524
00:32:05,056 --> 00:32:06,858
I will not sit here and do nothing,

525
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,427
knowing you have a gauzeoma.

526
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:11,162
But...

527
00:32:12,730 --> 00:32:15,099
if it doesn't go well,
I will die, won't I?

528
00:32:15,166 --> 00:32:16,334
Not really.

529
00:32:19,504 --> 00:32:20,872
Because I never fail.

530
00:32:26,511 --> 00:32:29,714
As planned, the surgery will begin
tomorrow at 10 a.m.

531
00:32:30,214 --> 00:32:31,816
Here, sign on it.

532
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:35,353
Until now, I've done many absurd things,

533
00:32:37,388 --> 00:32:39,257
but this may be the chance
to start afresh.

534
00:32:43,361 --> 00:32:47,932
I…plan to start with a clean slate.

535
00:32:57,575 --> 00:32:59,944
Wasn't that a long time to just
get her signature?

536
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:01,713
What were you talking about?

537
00:33:02,246 --> 00:33:04,782
I have a duty as her physician
to keep her privacy.

538
00:33:06,584 --> 00:33:09,721
What did she say?

539
00:33:11,789 --> 00:33:15,760
She wants to start with a clean slate.

540
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:23,401
Start with…a clean slate?

541
00:33:36,114 --> 00:33:38,583
We should remove the gauze...

542
00:33:38,649 --> 00:33:41,953
without rupturing the artery.

543
00:33:42,387 --> 00:33:44,022
That sounds difficult.

544
00:33:44,088 --> 00:33:46,924
Moreover, shouldn't Dr. Saionji...

545
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,795
assist the surgery at least?

546
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:53,898
If he did something so ridiculous,
I would be off the surgery.

547
00:33:53,965 --> 00:33:56,634
He's only ridiculous as a person, right?

548
00:33:57,568 --> 00:33:59,170
The operation room is ready.

549
00:33:59,237 --> 00:34:00,338
Got it.

550
00:34:07,812 --> 00:34:09,647
OPERATION IN PROGRESS

551
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:14,452
Anaesthesia is administered...

552
00:34:14,519 --> 00:34:16,020
and her vitals are stable.

553
00:34:28,199 --> 00:34:30,401
We will now begin the surgery
to remove the tumour

554
00:34:30,468 --> 00:34:33,271
and to replace the abdominal aorta
with an artificial vessel.

555
00:34:33,337 --> 00:34:34,238
Let's get started.

556
00:34:34,305 --> 00:34:35,406
Yes.

557
00:34:36,974 --> 00:34:38,209
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

558
00:35:07,638 --> 00:35:09,707
Please lower the magnifier...

559
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:10,842
on my goggles.

560
00:35:11,175 --> 00:35:13,778
Excuse me.

561
00:35:13,845 --> 00:35:15,179
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Yes.

562
00:35:28,726 --> 00:35:29,927
Lastly, Doctor Saionji.

563
00:35:30,361 --> 00:35:31,529
Yes?

564
00:35:31,596 --> 00:35:36,901
Isn't this…what you're thinking now?

565
00:35:37,335 --> 00:35:38,169
What?

566
00:35:38,236 --> 00:35:41,973
"Michiko Daimon," mess up the operation.

567
00:35:47,078 --> 00:35:48,212
But...

568
00:35:49,914 --> 00:35:54,318
what's frustrating…is that she never

569
00:35:55,453 --> 00:35:59,490
makes mistake at all. I almost envy her.

570
00:36:00,691 --> 00:36:02,026
What do you think?

571
00:36:04,495 --> 00:36:05,496
Misae said...

572
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:11,836
- she wants to start with a clean slate.
- What?

573
00:36:11,903 --> 00:36:18,342
Perhaps, after she gets discharged,
she will prosecute me.

574
00:36:18,409 --> 00:36:22,146
How dreadful! Unbelievable.

575
00:36:22,213 --> 00:36:24,715
She'll make everything public.

576
00:36:24,782 --> 00:36:28,119
That's bad!

577
00:36:31,589 --> 00:36:33,024
- What?
- Please help me.

578
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:34,825
- What?
- Please.

579
00:36:34,892 --> 00:36:38,162
I can only settle this with money.

580
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,831
Money to keep her quiet?

581
00:36:40,898 --> 00:36:41,799
Please!

582
00:36:42,433 --> 00:36:47,405
Please! Please do anything you can
to collect money and lend it to me!

583
00:36:47,471 --> 00:36:50,107
Hey, hey, hey...

584
00:36:50,174 --> 00:36:52,577
- Please. Please!
- I...

585
00:36:52,643 --> 00:36:54,478
Wait, the operation is over.

586
00:36:56,514 --> 00:36:58,449
The gauzeoma has been removed.

587
00:36:58,516 --> 00:37:00,952
- Let's close.
- Look at her.

588
00:37:01,018 --> 00:37:04,522
Michiko Daimon, full of confidence.

589
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:18,035
With this, the blood vessel
will not rupture.

590
00:37:20,371 --> 00:37:21,505
Finished.

591
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:23,674
Vitals are 111 and 76.

592
00:37:33,284 --> 00:37:34,418
This is only the beginning.

593
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,521
- Nice work.
- Good job.

594
00:37:38,789 --> 00:37:39,690
Good work.

595
00:38:07,918 --> 00:38:09,253
50,000 dollars.

596
00:38:17,628 --> 00:38:18,963
Hello.

597
00:38:19,697 --> 00:38:20,765
Hello.

598
00:38:21,432 --> 00:38:24,201
I heard you are being discharged today.

599
00:38:25,770 --> 00:38:29,540
I feel horrible about everything.

600
00:38:29,607 --> 00:38:31,042
I hope this...

601
00:38:31,108 --> 00:38:32,443
What a timing.

602
00:38:33,544 --> 00:38:36,681
I was going…to visit you anyway.

603
00:38:36,747 --> 00:38:37,882
Oh, okay.

604
00:38:38,616 --> 00:38:39,550
Here you go.

605
00:38:39,617 --> 00:38:41,419
CHEQUE FOR 200,000 DOLLARS

606
00:38:44,188 --> 00:38:45,323
200,000 dollars?

607
00:38:48,192 --> 00:38:49,427
Honestly,

608
00:38:49,860 --> 00:38:53,364
I'm running as a candidate for governor
in the next Tokyo election.

609
00:38:53,431 --> 00:38:54,298
Governor...

610
00:38:54,365 --> 00:38:55,599
Governor?

611
00:38:57,601 --> 00:39:02,073
Actually, after you dumped me...
I changed my job.

612
00:39:03,441 --> 00:39:05,476
I made many connections
to the political world.

613
00:39:05,976 --> 00:39:07,011
I see.

614
00:39:07,078 --> 00:39:09,447
So, this is a hush money.

615
00:39:10,214 --> 00:39:11,048
What?

616
00:39:11,115 --> 00:39:15,319
The fact that we were lovers in the past
must not be revealed to the public.

617
00:39:17,855 --> 00:39:20,224
It is a chance for me,

618
00:39:20,691 --> 00:39:24,462
so I want to become a governor
and give Tokyo a clean slate.

619
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:27,031
A clean slate means...

620
00:39:27,098 --> 00:39:29,367
A very important time is about to begin.

621
00:39:29,433 --> 00:39:32,069
I don't want such things
become made public.

622
00:39:32,136 --> 00:39:34,205
- You get it, right?
- Yes.

623
00:39:34,271 --> 00:39:36,741
I don't want to lose because
of an insignificant man...

624
00:39:37,074 --> 00:39:38,209
from my past.

625
00:39:39,677 --> 00:39:41,712
An insignificant man?

626
00:39:47,918 --> 00:39:53,858
Do you think that women dumped
by men can never be happy?

627
00:39:56,026 --> 00:40:00,765
Well, don't let what happened
in the past bother you.

628
00:40:02,733 --> 00:40:07,705
But if that gets in my way,
it must be gotten rid of.

629
00:40:10,574 --> 00:40:11,609
See you.

630
00:40:11,675 --> 00:40:12,510
Bye!

631
00:40:16,046 --> 00:40:18,382
Hey!

632
00:40:18,449 --> 00:40:19,283
Hey!

633
00:40:19,617 --> 00:40:21,252
Wait!

634
00:40:21,585 --> 00:40:24,688
Wait a minute.

635
00:40:25,723 --> 00:40:27,391
An insignificant man?

636
00:40:32,062 --> 00:40:36,000
An insignificant man?

637
00:40:52,416 --> 00:40:53,617
200,000 dollars?

638
00:40:54,885 --> 00:40:58,756
- You got this from her as a hush money?
- Yes.

639
00:40:59,990 --> 00:41:01,725
I really underestimated her.

640
00:41:07,364 --> 00:41:09,233
It's because you had no clue.

641
00:41:09,667 --> 00:41:10,501
Yes.

642
00:41:10,568 --> 00:41:12,203
CHEQUE FOR 200,000 DOLLARS

643
00:41:16,273 --> 00:41:17,308
What?

644
00:41:17,374 --> 00:41:21,212
What? This is a hush money.

645
00:41:21,278 --> 00:41:22,646
It's mine.

646
00:41:22,713 --> 00:41:26,717
- No, I'm the one who should be silent.
- But that's...

647
00:41:29,220 --> 00:41:30,621
Stop the car.

648
00:41:36,060 --> 00:41:37,528
Hello!

649
00:41:38,896 --> 00:41:44,301
Because you picked this up for me,
I was able to become refreshed...

650
00:41:44,368 --> 00:41:47,137
and sort out things from my past.

651
00:41:47,204 --> 00:41:48,105
I'm so glad.

652
00:41:48,772 --> 00:41:50,274
You're lying, right?

653
00:41:50,875 --> 00:41:54,845
I know you always...
carried the wallet with you.

654
00:41:55,513 --> 00:41:58,215
- What?
- It was a present from him, right?

655
00:42:02,219 --> 00:42:05,689
Sorry, when I picked it up
I looked inside.

656
00:42:09,827 --> 00:42:11,896
It's not my business though.

657
00:42:14,932 --> 00:42:18,369
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

658
00:42:46,497 --> 00:42:48,465
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

659
00:42:49,199 --> 00:42:53,470
<i>Despising the herd mentality,</i>
<i>authority and institutional restraints...</i>

660
00:42:54,338 --> 00:42:57,374
<i>Her solo weapons are her license and</i>

661
00:42:57,841 --> 00:42:59,043
<i>the skills she has earned.</i>

662
00:43:00,377 --> 00:43:01,579
Here is a melon.

663
00:43:02,179 --> 00:43:03,180
Here is a bill.

664
00:43:07,284 --> 00:43:09,019
What? 250,000 dollars?

665
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:11,889
80 percent of the billed amount...

666
00:43:11,956 --> 00:43:14,992
is given to Dr. Saionji as a hush money.

667
00:43:15,059 --> 00:43:16,193
Yes, but...

668
00:43:16,827 --> 00:43:18,228
Wait. Under here.

669
00:43:18,862 --> 00:43:20,798
- Excuse me.
- What?

670
00:43:20,864 --> 00:43:22,366
Oh my!

671
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:24,368
You've already prepared it.

672
00:43:26,437 --> 00:43:29,340
Do you have…a third eye?

673
00:43:31,742 --> 00:43:32,643
You do. Got it!

674
00:43:42,519 --> 00:43:44,989
A huge success!

675
00:43:48,993 --> 00:43:51,261
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

676
00:43:51,695 --> 00:43:52,696
<i>Also known as</i>

677
00:43:54,098 --> 00:43:55,366
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

678
00:45:14,044 --> 00:45:16,480
A double operation? I can't do both.

679
00:45:16,547 --> 00:45:18,348
I'm a charismatic woman.

680
00:45:18,415 --> 00:45:20,651
If I don't lose my weight,
it will all be over for Yotsuba sisters.

681
00:45:20,718 --> 00:45:24,088
That is not the only reason
why I called for you.

682
00:45:24,154 --> 00:45:26,123
You're only an assistant!

683
00:45:26,190 --> 00:45:28,425
I never fail, even as an assistant.
